# Trivy CVE allowlist for the OCI Platform image scans.
#
# Each entry MUST include:
#  - CVE ID
#  - the affected package and current vs. fixed version
#  - the rationale (why exploitability is low for our workload)
#  - a tracking note for when to revisit
#
# Entries are revisited every 30 days; if a fix has reached our base
# image we MUST remove the suppression. Open a Phase A2 follow-up
# issue to refresh the base image when distroless ships the patch.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# libssl3 (Debian 12 / distroless gcr.io/distroless/nodejs24-debian12)
# Installed: 3.0.18-1~deb12u2
# Fixed:     3.0.20-1~deb12u2 (still not in the distroless image as of 2026-06-11;
#            distroless remains on 3.0.18 — it has lagged both the .19 and .20 bumps)
# Rationale: the NestJS API container only handles inbound HTTP from
# CloudFront/ALB (TLS terminated upstream) and outbound TLS to AWS
# service endpoints. It does not validate arbitrary X.509 client
# certificates, does not implement DANE TLSA, and does not parse
# CMS payloads. The OpenSSL surface area exposed by these CVEs is
# not reachable.
# Mitigation: rebuild and re-deploy as soon as distroless publishes
# the libssl3 update.
CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2026-28387
CVE-2026-28388
CVE-2026-28389
CVE-2026-28390
# Added 2026-06-11: CVE-2026-45447 (libssl3 HIGH) — crafted PKCS#7 / S/MIME
# (CMS) signed-message parsing. Same package and the same unreachable surface
# as the block above (the API parses no CMS payloads; TLS is terminated
# upstream). Fix 3.0.20-1~deb12u2 is not yet in the distroless base, and the
# HIGH gate was blocking all deploys. Remove when distroless ships the patch —
# the scheduled suppression audit will flag it.
CVE-2026-45447

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# undici (npm) — image scan only (build-images), not the CI filesystem scan.
# Installed: 6.26.0    Fixed: 6.27.0
# CVE-2026-12151: DoS via unbounded memory growth over WebSocket.
# Why suppressed: undici is a *devDependency* of transitives (hono,
# light-my-request, oauth4webapi) — NOT a runtime dependency. It leaks into
# app/node_modules via `pnpm deploy --prod --legacy` (a prod-isolate bug),
# and the API never uses undici's WebSocket *client* (it is an HTTP server;
# outbound calls go through the AWS SDK). The DoS surface is not reachable.
# A pnpm.overrides pin to undici ^6.27.0 exists but does NOT reach the
# --legacy isolate, so it can't fix the image on its own.
# Root-cause fix (stop shipping devDeps in the prod image) tracked separately;
# remove this once that lands. Scheduled suppression audit will flag it.
CVE-2026-12151

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Removed 2026-05-26: the scheduled Trivy suppression audit confirmed
# both CVE-2026-33671 (picomatch in the Prisma CLI tarball) and
# CVE-2026-0861 (libc6 in distroless/nodejs24-debian12) are no longer
# reported by a fresh scan — upstream fixes have shipped. See
# .github/workflows/trivy-suppression-audit.yml + the artefact at
# https://github.com/FG-AI4H/oci-platform/actions/runs/26445163973.
# Re-add if the next image build surfaces them again.
